    "reason": "The assertion 'retrieval precision equals relevant passages count' is logically false because precision is a ratio (numerator/denominator), not the numerator itself. Equating a derived metric to one of its components ignores the divisor (total retrieved). The correct relation must express that precision is calculated by dividing the count of relevant passages by the total count of returned passages.",
